null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097562,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1NjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:android","name":"platform:android","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-22T04:31:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T09:25:50Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T01:52:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nall\n\n### System information\n\nAll Android - Google Play Store\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhenever a new update of Godot is released, the Google Play Store automatically publishes it.\n\nRight now, the latest stable version is Godot 4.6.2, but the Play Store is showing Godot 4.7 Beta\n\nThe problem becomes worse when another stable update is released. For example, if **Godot 4.6.3** comes out, the Play Store version changes from 4.7 Beta back to 4.6.3.\n\nThis creates confusion because:\n\n* Beta versions should usually stay in a separate beta/testing channel.\n* Stable releases should not replace beta builds unexpectedly.\n* The version order appears inconsistent to users.\n\nIn short, the Play Store is not handling stable and beta release tracks properly.\n\nAnd If someone want to test the beda version we can allow user to become a beta tester\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nGodot Android Editor","closed_by":{"login":"llama-nl","id":94882246,"node_id":"U_kgDOBafJxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94882246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/llama-nl","html_url":"https://github.com/llama-nl","followers_url":"https://api.githu